SUMMARY:AYPROS SEPTEMBER Pub Club: New Belgium
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\nFew places make a bett
 er backdrop for an AYPROS Pub Club than a brewery overlooking the French B
 road River.\nJoin AYPROS on **Tuesday\, September 22** for our September P
 ub Club at **New Belgium Brewing**\, where we’ll spend the evening at th
 eir riverside Asheville brewery and Liquid Center on Craven Street.\nNew B
 elgium has been part of Asheville’s beer scene for a decade\, but the se
 tting alone makes it worth another visit. The 18-acre brewery sits along t
 he French Broad River\, with a 6\,000-square-foot riverside taproom\, plen
 ty of indoor and outdoor space\, and furniture and design elements created
  from repurposed materials and work by local artists.\nIn other words\, it
  is pretty much built for Pub Club.\n\nWhether this is your first AYPROS e
 vent or you know half the room already\, Pub Club is meant to be easy. Lea
 ve the business cards at home. There is no presentation\, no agenda and no
  expectation that you have to work the room. Grab a drink\, find a spot by
  the river\, catch up with some familiar faces and introduce yourself to s
 omebody new.\n\nWe’ll be there from **5:00 PM - 8:00 PM**\, and\, as alw
 ays\, Pub Club is come-and-go. Show up when you can and stay as long as yo
 u’d like.\n\nYour **first drink is on us**\, courtesy of our Pub Club Ti
 tle Sponsor\, **Allen Stahl + Kilbourne (ASK Law)**.\n\nNew Belgium will h
 ave its lineup of beers and other beverage options available throughout th
 e evening\, and **The Smokin’ Onion** is scheduled to be onsite serving 
 its scratch-made\, plant-based food for anyone looking to grab dinner.\n\n
 ## What to Expect\n\n* A relaxed\, come-and-go evening along the French Br
 oad River\n* Your first drink included courtesy of ASK Law\n* Additional b
 everages available for purchase\n* Food available for purchase from The Sm
 okin’ Onion\n* Indoor and outdoor seating at New Belgium’s Asheville L
 iquid Center\n* Plenty of time to catch up with friends and meet other you
 ng professionals\n* First-time attendees and people coming on their own ar
 e absolutely welcome\n* No formal program or speeches\n\n## Schedule\n\n**
 5:00 PM** \\- Check\\-in opens\\\, first drinks and Pub Club begins\n**8:0
 0 PM** \\- AYPROS Pub Club concludes\n\n## Location\n\n**New Belgium Brewi
 ng**\n21 Craven Street\nAsheville\, NC 28806\n\n## Parking\n\nNew Belgium 
 offers **street parking near the brewery as well as two onsite parking lot
 s**. Please do not park in the gravel production lot behind the brewery.\n
 Come when you can\, find us by the river\, grab your first drink and spend
  an early fall evening with Asheville’s young professional community at 
 one of the city’s best-known brewery destinations.\nA special thank you 
 to **New Belgium Brewing** for welcoming AYPROS and to **Allen Stahl + Kil
 bourne (ASK Law)** for continuing to make Pub Club possible by picking up 
 everyone’s first drink.\nWe’ll see you by the river.
